<title>POLAND: Polish broad money rises 1.7 pct in April 1-10.</title>
<headline>Polish broad money rises 1.7 pct in April 1-10.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money rose by 2.39 billion zlotys, or 1.7 percent, in April 1-10 to 143.90 billion after a 2.2 percent rise in the whole of March, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Broad money supply grew 5.9 percent in the January-April 10 period against 8.3 percent in the same period of last year.</p>
</text>
